Wang <italic>et al. </italic>[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B20">20</xref>] and Conlon <italic>et al. </italic>[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B21">21</xref>] previously fit regression models using sequence features derived from <italic>S. cerevisiae</italic>. The <italic>p</italic>-values of the most similar sequences features in their regression models were reported where available; sequence features that were more significant in this analysis are indicated in bold. Dashes indicate sequence features that were insignificant in the Wang <italic>et al. </italic>[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B20">20</xref>] or Conlon <italic>et al. </italic>[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B21">21</xref>] analyses. 'N/R' indicates gene-expression data that were not analyzed by Conlon <italic>et al. </italic>[<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="B21">21</xref>]</p></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></sec></back></article>